WEBVTT

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.976
their valuable political
and social capital on you,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.056
this person who is going
to pound the table on your behalf,

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.560
this is a sponsor.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.040
This is a sponsor."

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.936
And then I said to myself,

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.496
"Well, how do you get a sponsor?

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.136
And frankly, why do you need one?"

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:21.936
Well, you need a sponsor, frankly,

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.336
because as you can see,

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:26.656
there's not one evaluative process
that I can think of,

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.296
whether it's in academia,
health care, financial services,